==============================================================================
Modifications in this fork

CourseClock is adapted for Shanghai University of Engineering Science (SUES)
only. Changes relative to the upstream work:

* Every school import path other than SUES was removed, together with its
  parsers, activities, layouts and resources.
* Added a SUES importer that guides the user through the university WebVPN and
  unified identity authentication, then reads the semester date range, the
  class times and the courses from the teaching service system.
* Modelled the campus per-building class times, selected by building, instead of
  a single table for the whole campus.
* Render the schedule on a real-time vertical axis: a course is positioned by its
  start time and sized by its duration, and courses that overlap in time are laid
  out side by side.
* Removed the donation and paid-unlock screens, the update check, the upstream
  service client and the App Center telemetry SDK, the promotion of an unrelated
  application, and the upstream customer-service links.
* Renamed the application and replaced every artwork asset — launcher icon
  (adaptive and legacy), notification icon, drawer icons, splash logo, widget
  preview, empty-state and network-error illustrations — with original minimal
  assets. The artwork sources are in design/.
* Replaced the default main-screen background photo with a flat colour: pure
  white, and pure black in dark mode. A user-chosen background image is still
  supported; it is loaded by the in-tree `BackgroundImageLoader` instead of the
  upstream Glide pipeline.
* Added a first-run notice stating the upstream origin and version, the
  Apache License 2.0 terms, and that the software is free of charge. A copy of
  the license and of this notice ships inside the APK under assets/.
